#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:1
msgid "Release 1.2 (2012-12-06)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:3
msgid "This release has the following improvements and changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:5
msgid ""
"Nix has a new binary substituter mechanism: the _binary cache_. A binary "
"cache contains pre-built binaries of Nix packages. Whenever Nix wants to "
"build a missing Nix store path, it will check a set of binary caches to see "
"if any of them has a pre-built binary of that path. The configuration "
"setting `binary-caches` contains a list of URLs of binary caches. For "
"instance, doing"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:12
msgid ""
"    $ nix-env -i thunderbird --option binary-caches http://cache.nixos.org\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:14
msgid ""
"will install Thunderbird and its dependencies, using the available pre-built "
"binaries in <http://cache.nixos.org>. The main advantage over the old "
"“manifest”-based method of getting pre-built binaries is that you don’t have "
"to worry about your manifest being in sync with the Nix expressions you’re "
"installing from; i.e., you don’t need to run `nix-pull` to update your "
"manifest. It’s also more scalable because you don’t need to redownload a "
"giant manifest file every time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:23
msgid ""
"A Nix channel can provide a binary cache URL that will be used automatically "
"if you subscribe to that channel. If you use the Nixpkgs or NixOS channels "
"(<http://nixos.org/channels>) you automatically get the cache <http://cache."
"nixos.org>."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:28
msgid ""
"Binary caches are created using `nix-push`. For details on the operation and "
"format of binary caches, see the `nix-push` manpage. More details are "
"provided in [this nix-dev posting](https://nixos.org/nix-dev/2012-"
"September/009826.html)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:33
msgid ""
"Multiple output support should now be usable. A derivation can declare that "
"it wants to produce multiple store paths by saying something like"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:37
msgid ""
"    outputs = [ \"lib\" \"headers\" \"doc\" ];\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:39
msgid ""
"This will cause Nix to pass the intended store path of each output to the "
"builder through the environment variables `lib`, `headers` and `doc`. Other "
"packages can refer to a specific output by referring to `pkg.output`, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:46
msgid ""
"If you install a package with multiple outputs using `nix-env`, each output "
"path will be symlinked into the user environment."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:49
msgid "Dashes are now valid as part of identifiers and attribute names."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:51
msgid ""
"The new operation `nix-store --repair-path` allows corrupted or missing "
"store paths to be repaired by redownloading them. `nix-store --verify --"
"check-contents                 --repair` will scan and repair all paths in "
"the Nix store. Similarly, `nix-env`, `nix-build`, `nix-instantiate` and `nix-"
"store --realise` have a `--repair` flag to detect and fix bad paths by "
"rebuilding or redownloading them."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:59
msgid ""
"Nix no longer sets the immutable bit on files in the Nix store. Instead, the "
"recommended way to guard the Nix store against accidental modification on "
"Linux is to make it a read-only bind mount, like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:67
msgid ""
"Nix will automatically make `/nix/store` writable as needed (using a private "
"mount namespace) to allow modifications."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:70
msgid ""
"Store optimisation (replacing identical files in the store with hard links) "
"can now be done automatically every time a path is added to the store. This "
"is enabled by setting the configuration option `auto-optimise-store` to "
"`true` (disabled by default)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:75
msgid ""
"Nix now supports `xz` compression for NARs in addition to `bzip2`. It "
"compresses about 30% better on typical archives and decompresses about twice "
"as fast."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:79
msgid ""
"Basic Nix expression evaluation profiling: setting the environment variable "
"`NIX_COUNT_CALLS` to `1` will cause Nix to print how many times each primop "
"or function was executed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:83
msgid "New primops: `concatLists`, `elem`, `elemAt` and `filter`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:85
msgid ""
"The command `nix-copy-closure` has a new flag `--use-substitutes` (`-s`) to "
"download missing paths on the target machine using the substitute mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:89
msgid ""
"The command `nix-worker` has been renamed to `nix-daemon`. Support for "
"running the Nix worker in “slave” mode has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:92
msgid "The `--help` flag of every Nix command now invokes `man`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:94
msgid "Chroot builds are now supported on systemd machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:96
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Eelco Dolstra, Florian Friesdorf, Mats "
"Erik Andersson and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""
